-- a definition: its type is a type, its term has that type
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- multiplicities (PLAN.md revision 7.9, 6 Nov 2026, git 2ca8d747aaa5:PLAN.md, §18.1 “B11 — Multiplicities (static side)”)
-- The usages of variables xs in a term, a list of words 0, 1, 2 (ω) along xs: 1 + 1 = ω, ω + _ = ω;
-- a join for alternatives; an argument counts as many times as the function's binder says. Types
-- (the A of a binder, a universe, a path type, an annotation) count nothing; a Glue system counts
-- ω. One walk gives every binder's usage.
-- Through the composition clauses (PLAN.md revision 7.9, 6 Nov 2026, git 2ca8d747aaa5:PLAN.md, §15 “Open threads”, the thread “Multiplicities over cubical paths”): the line a comp runs along is read for what
-- its computation reads (lusage): a path type's endpoints become the sides of the composition in
-- it and count ω, a Glue's or a universe composition's system counts ω (its equivalences run), a
-- data type's parameter that is a type is read as a line again and any other parameter counts ω
-- (it can reach a field's path endpoints), an application of a family counts ω (it unfolds to who
-- knows what); a variable in type position counts nothing, so a binder at 0 used only as the type
-- a transport runs along stays erasable. The tube and the base are joined, not added: where both
-- are present they agree (u 0 = a on the tube's face), the composition's value on the face is the
-- tube's end and off it is built from the base, so a resource in both is one resource at its two
-- ends; a resource used twice within the base, or within one side, is still ω.
u+ a b = let s = %wadd a b in if %wlt s #2 then s else #2
